{"title":"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A Bauman number is a positive integer each of whose digits is 1 or 2. Each Bauman number consists of blocks of digits. Each block contains at least one digit and includes all of the consecutive equal digits. For example, 2222111112111 is a 13-digit Bauman number consisting of four blocks: a block of four 2s, then a block of five 1s, then a block of one 2, then a block of three 1s; 2222222 is a 7-digit Bauman number consisting of a single block of seven 2s.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many 3-digit Bauman numbers are there?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can list all of the integers with either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as digits that are also 3-digit numbers:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d1eed7be2e1dcbfd4f7fe86fba2eb7566d8bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3907e89ce5b06f13d78589b5d92624a8b41a7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$112$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76ad7692f5d86be790209a56a68c2a3488235054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/8/7a8948c71337e6ef8aac086dd7444c757c379b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$122$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/7651217ecd64cc60cbd7805a091340edeef83281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$211$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67ff4304a3602b8aac31124d7ce9b035d1b89e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$212$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/155fa3807f26f4268430319bb47b97658353ad8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$222$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Counting all of these numbers, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81ca9c5c8715be868438500743202d6773d05bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices for each digit since each digit can either be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, the number of 3-digit Bauman numbers would be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953e7bf7190ce0a6df1e3374118122ba2b43b000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3} = \\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"63\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005330\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.015 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 83/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 538/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2741/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.227      1 2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%    6.227      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35562:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005330 and revision id 277966. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}